   "widgets_values": [
    "Medieval dark fantasy comic art by Frank Quitely. Very wide establishing shot, perpendicular framing. At bottom right of frame, we see in profile the small figure of a knight in plate armor and a white tabard riding a black horse down a shadowy trail. Two other knights in plain blue cloaks carrying spears on brown horses follow him at bottom left. In the background, a steep rocky wooded hillside towers over them, dominating the frame. At upper left, we see a small patch of blue sky; at upper right, the sky is dark. In the center of the frame, superimposed, we see a locket featuring an oil painting portrait of a gorgeous young dark-haired woman. She has a faint, sweet smile. On the frame of the locket, along the top we see the following inscription: \"To Sir Galedh, my devoted protector\"; along the bottom: \"Forever your songbird\". The locket has a hinge on the left and a clasp on the right. The white cloth background against the locket gradually fades into the image of the knights in the woods."
   ]
